{{Term/Store|Blue Nightshade|Blue Nightshades|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Blue Nightshade}}
Blue Nightshades can be found growing in the [[Region]]s of [[West Necluda]] and [[Lanayru Great Spring]] in [[Hyrule Kingdom]]. Many Blue Nightshades grow near [[Cotera's Great Fairy Fountain]] outside of [[Kakariko Village]]. These [[Flower]]s glow at night, making them easier to find. When Blue Nightshade is [[Cooking|Cooked]] into a [[Meal]] in a [[Cooking Pot]], it will grant [[Link]] [[Stealth Up]] when eaten.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> At the [[Kochi Dye Shop]], Link can use Blue Nightshades to make [[Blue Dye]].

As part of the [[Side Quest]] "[[A Gift of Nightshade]]", Link must give [[Wabbin]] a Blue Nightshade that he can gift to [[Perda]].<ref name="BotW Wabbin"/> However, once he obtains one, Wabbin will become nervous and ask Link to deliver the Blue Nightshade on his behalf.<ref name="BotW Wabbin 2"/> After he does this, Perda will confront Wabbin, asking how he knew that Blue Nightshades were her favorite Flower.<ref name="BotW Perda"/> Wabbin reveals that Blue Nightshades are his favorite Flowers as well, and he decided he would give them to his true love.<ref name="BotW Wabbin 3"/> Once the two of them confess their feelings, Wabbin will give Link 20 [[Rupee]]s.

